author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "No fenced command-position invocation in agent-facing markdown instructs a spelling the alias table marks deprecated, and the canonical replacement is named in the failure when one does; The deprecated set the check iterates is read from the shipped alias table rather than restated, so a newly deprecated spelling is covered without editing the check; The gate's own required markers use canonical spellings, so conforming content cannot fail and deprecated content cannot pass; A negative control proves the check fails when one deprecated instruction is reintroduced, and a second control proves it refuses to pass vacuously when the alias table is empty; Prose that documents the alias compatibility contract remains permitted, because recording that a spelling still executes is not an instruction to type it; The documented preference and the alias table agree on which spelling is canonical"
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Agent-facing markdown instructs only canonical command spellings, and a reintroduced deprecated instruction fails a gate that already runs."
actual_result: 27 instructions across 19 files rewritten; the gate's own two enforcement sites repaired; the new check passes with both a negative and a vacuous-pass control proven.
