comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T11:29:31.763Z","harness:claude-code","Fixed and gated in one pass on 2026-08-30.\n\nRewrote all 27 fenced command-position invocations across 19 files to canonical spellings: pm install -> pm package install, pm upgrade -> pm package upgrade, pm extension -> pm package, pm list-open -> pm list --status open. Flag-style package actions introduced by the rewrite were normalised to subcommand form (pm package doctor, pm package reload, pm package install). Every replacement was executed against a sandbox tracker before editing, so no doc now instructs a command that does not run.\n\nReconciled docs/COMMANDS.md: the preference sentence now names pm package as canonical and states that pm install, pm upgrade and pm extension remain executable deprecated compatibility spellings that must not appear as instructions. Five inline instruction occurrences in the same file were rewritten.\n\nThe gate itself was pointing the wrong way and had to be repaired before the check could be added: two enforcement sites required the literal string 'pm install guide-shell', so a skill written canonically failed and a skill written deprecated passed. Both now reference a single GUIDE_SHELL_INSTALL_MARKER constant holding the canonical spelling.\n\nNew check validateDeprecatedCommandSpellings reads the deprecated set from the built SDK's PM_COMMAND_ALIAS_CONTRACTS by dynamic import rather than restating it, scans only fenced blocks in command position so prose documenting the compatibility contract stays legal, and names the canonical replacement in each failure.\n\nControls, both run:\n- Negative control: reintroducing pm install guide-shell --project into AGENTS.md fails with 'AGENTS.md:22: instructs deprecated command spelling pm install; use pm package install'; restoring the canonical spelling passes.\n- Vacuous-pass control: an empty alias table makes the check fail with an explicit message rather than passing, so the check cannot silently stop enforcing if the table is ever unreadable.\n\nUnit coverage added for extractFencedPmInvocations fence and command-position boundaries, for the alias-table mapping including the property that a permanent alias such as show is not flagged, for the positive detection path, and for the vacuous-pass guard. docs-skills-gate.spec.ts 27 passed; the gate passes end to end."
